From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:02:51 +0800
Subject: net: stmmac: tc956x: Reserve more RX FIFO headroom for ASPM

On the Q8B with a TC956x and a 2.5 Gb/s PHY, enabling PCIe ASPM L1
substates causes receive FIFO overflows and TCP retransmissions. The
8 KiB RX queues assert PAUSE with only 3 KiB of free space. This leaves
insufficient room for in-flight frames while the receive DMA resumes
after a low-power state.

Add a platform-specific RX flow-control headroom setting and request
4 KiB for TC956x. Apply it when programming the XGMAC RX queue thresholds,
keeping a positive deactivation threshold and at least 512 bytes of
hysteresis. Leave the existing defaults unchanged for other platforms.
For the TC956x 8 KiB queues, raise RFA from 4 to 6 and keep RFD at 7.

Signed-off-by: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
Link: https://vamrs.feishu.cn/docx/L4zydgTkvor8xlxUInlcrEhFnRg
(cherry picked from commit b0a5929032174ae0ead5d6a2876ef71754f63461)
[SuperKali: adapted to Linux 7.3]
Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tc956x.c |  2 ++
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwxgmac2_dma.c | 10 ++++++++++
 include/linux/stmmac.h                             |  2 ++
 3 files changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tc956x.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tc956x.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tc956x.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tc956x.c
@@ -662,6 +662,8 @@ static int tc956x_plat_dat_init(struct tc956x_data *td)
 		min(TC956X_TX_FIFO_KB, 8 * plat->tx_queues_to_use) * SZ_1K;
 	plat->rx_fifo_size =
 		min(TC956X_RX_FIFO_KB, 8 * plat->rx_queues_to_use) * SZ_1K;
+	/* Cover in-flight frames while PCIe exits an ASPM low-power state. */
+	plat->rx_fifo_flow_ctrl_headroom = SZ_4K;
 	plat->host_dma_width = 36;
 
 	plat->rx_sched_algorithm = MTL_RX_ALGORITHM_SP;
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwxgmac2_dma.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwxgmac2_dma.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwxgmac2_dma.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwxgmac2_dma.c
@@ -160,6 +160,7 @@ static void dwxgmac2_dma_rx_mode(struct stmmac_priv *priv, void __iomem *ioaddr,
 	if ((fifosz >= 4096) && (qmode != MTL_QUEUE_AVB)) {
 		u32 flow = readl(ioaddr + XGMAC_MTL_RXQ_FLOW_CONTROL(channel));
 		unsigned int rfd, rfa;
+		unsigned int headroom = priv->plat->rx_fifo_flow_ctrl_headroom;
 
 		value |= XGMAC_EHFC;
 
@@ -184,6 +185,15 @@ static void dwxgmac2_dma_rx_mode(struct stmmac_priv *priv, void __iomem *ioaddr,
 			break;
 		}
 
+		/* Leave room for packets arriving while the receive DMA wakes up.
+		 * Keep a positive deactivation threshold and at least 512 bytes
+		 * of hysteresis. Platforms without an override keep the defaults.
+		 */
+		if (headroom >= 1024 && headroom <= fifosz - 1024) {
+			rfa = max(rfa, DIV_ROUND_UP(headroom, 512) - 2);
+			rfd = max(rfd, rfa + 1);
+		}
+
 		flow = u32_replace_bits(flow, rfd, XGMAC_RFD);
 		flow = u32_replace_bits(flow, rfa, XGMAC_RFA);
 
diff --git a/include/linux/stmmac.h b/include/linux/stmmac.h
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/include/linux/stmmac.h
+++ b/include/linux/stmmac.h
@@ -264,6 +264,8 @@ struct plat_stmmacenet_data {
 	int unicast_filter_entries;
 	int tx_fifo_size;
 	int rx_fifo_size;
+	/* Minimum free RX FIFO space when hardware flow control is asserted. */
+	unsigned int rx_fifo_flow_ctrl_headroom;
 	u8 host_dma_width;
 	u8 rx_queues_to_use;
 	u8 tx_queues_to_use;
-- 
Armbian

